00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:21.200
Because I think this is a point in favor of the game for me, that there are, like, bad

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:22.920
power-ups. We haven't seen that yet.

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:25.860
Like, where even your power-ups might be your enemy.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:32.020
Right. Well, I just feel like the sprite artist woke up the morning, he was going to turn in all

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:33.700
his sprites, and he was like, oh, shit.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:35.320
Like, what about the power-ups?

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:38.500
And he was like, all right, we'll just do, like, the letter, the initial in a square.

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:41.040
Like, it just felt a little rushed.

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:46.180
Okay. And then we were talking about missiles versus shooting, and I kind of wanted to get back

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:53.240
to that, because we have had that a few times now in Shmup-style games, where missiles are

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:59.060
used for ground combat, and then you also shoot in the air at other things, so you kind of

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:03.740
have to differentiate between what's something you can shoot bullets at versus what do you

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:04.860
need to use missiles on.

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:07.380
Yeah. And in this game, I actually thought it was very well done.

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:09.820
I think it was very clear what was what.

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:14.960
I think that at this point, though, and I'll let you finish, but I think that it's a pretty

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:21.520
codified game mechanic, where it doesn't, it's sort of, like, expected with the package

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:27.120
now that there's going to be two different kinds of firing for if you're going from air

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:28.340
to ground or air to air.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:33.500
So I'm not going to give it too much credit, just because it's doing what other games have

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:38.260
done as well. Well, if you want me to give a shout-out where shout-outs do, I think it's back to 1942,

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:44.960
which did use the other button as a way to kind of dodge all combat for a little bit

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:46.880
of time, kind of reset your location.

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:53.140
You did a flip in the air, and for that point in time, you were completely invincible.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:57.140
Yeah. Wouldn't mind seeing, like, something like that return to the Shmup games again?

00:14:57.140 --> 00:15:02.200
We might not see that very often, because I think they kind of do need this differentiation

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:10.140
between, like, tanks, which clearly are not in the air, but are present in war, versus,

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:12.840
like, you know, other alien spaceships.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:43.140
Yeah. We'll be right back.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:15.020
And not slow down for your ship.

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:19.200
I'm talking about, you know, to Joe's point, frame rate drops.

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:22.100
Like, I didn't know that could happen in these NES games.

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:30.320
Not only are you just that slow and your power-ups don't even get you all that fast, but the game programming itself will make it even slower.

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:38.460
It's not – I don't know if it gets to pass because we've seen games that do the exact same thing and perform perfectly.

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:43.420
Yeah, Gradius had no difficulty emulating all that stuff and arguably looked better.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.100
Yeah. I mean, not arguably.

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:47.120
Yeah. Okay.

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:48.740
It just depends on your preference.

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:50.800
I guess. If you like jank-looking things.

00:16:52.180 --> 00:17:02.140
Well, there was like that – some of the alien spaceships looked like sea creatures in real life.

00:17:02.260 --> 00:17:08.480
Like there was that one that looked like the skeleton thing that you grab by the tail that's dead.

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:11.620
What the fuck?

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:12.660
This is a real life thing?

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:14.460
Yeah, yeah, yeah. It's a real life thing.

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:17.800
It's – Can we put a picture of this thing in the show notes?

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:19.900
Yeah, I don't – I know what you're talking about.

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:20.940
Okay, you know what I'm talking about.

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:22.020
It's that thing. Yeah.

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:23.780
What is that? Can I see?

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:25.360
No, no, no. You can't see.

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:26.960
It would be too much of me.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:34.020
No, it's fine. Look, it's not that I don't know the name, but like these things, they look a lot like sea creatures.

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:36.720
So I thought we were fighting bugs based on the box art.

00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:42.520
Then I find out we're – in the manual, we're fighting like a different – like a totally different galaxy altogether.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:45.740
But then the ships come in and they start looking like sea creatures again.

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:47.940
So who is this war really against?

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:50.600
I think we're playing scoon again.

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:53.760
Okay. Oh, you're right.

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:55.720
But in space. Shoot, I played scoon.

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:58.460
Yeah, yeah. We've been talking about scoon this whole time.

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:00.600
No. Okay.

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:06.040
Let's get away from the slowdown issues and many of the issues that we have in this game.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:15.260
I will point out that if you do suffer from slowdown, it doesn't make you – you would think that that would make you better at this game because you have more opportunities to like time out what you're going to do.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:18.740
But the slowdown affects you possibly even more than the ships.

00:18:18.980 --> 00:18:27.720
When things were – when I was having like flickering and frame problems, I was more susceptible to dying than I was shooting down the new super slow ships.

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:30.620
Well, yeah, because like the whole rhythm has changed now.

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:38.320
It's like you can't really – I mean they're going slow, but I can still see myself dying many times because of the slowdown.

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:41.480
It really throws you off your game.

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:46.620
And we talked about most of the items, but we didn't talk about this warp and reverse.

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:54.260
And so the warp one will bring you forward three like stages, which usually –

00:18:54.260 --> 00:19:01.160
Screens pretty much. Usually stages means like actual levels, but that doesn't happen really in this game.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:04.540
It's all just one kind of fluid experience, the game.

00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:07.400
And there's no story going on.

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:16.680
Well, I mean there is a – it does get broken up a bit because there will be a lot of background objects when you're just going through a level.

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:19.360
But once you get to the boss, it's just black space.

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:21.460
Right. So you know where like the division is.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:22.540
Yeah, you know where the division is.

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:26.940
And there is like a – it does pop up that says like level one or something.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:30.640
Oh, really? Okay. I guess I didn't pay attention to that because I thought that was strange.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:34.040
I remember thinking throughout the game, I was like, what's the progression system?

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:35.440
Is it just a high score?

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:36.840
Like – Pretty much.

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:38.380
Okay. But –

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:40.680
It's not beatable, right?

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:42.260
This game isn't – It doesn't end.

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:44.060
Yeah, it doesn't end and that's not great.

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:45.580
Yeah. I don't like games that don't end.

00:19:46.020 --> 00:19:47.860
So – Pac-Man even ends.

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:51.200
When it stops being able to compute itself.

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:56.240
But that's what – you know, Pac-Man is a metaphor for like hacking, so it would make sense, you know.

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:58.100
The whole – Yeah. Like it was meant to be.

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:04.080
Yeah. So let's get into the weapon select because I think that this is something that is pretty cool.

00:20:04.420 --> 00:20:07.380
Mm-hmm. But then the execution is terrible.

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:16.460
So with weapon selecting, other than like having your ship have like power-ups that continue to be added to it, we've seen in other games little mini ships come to your side.

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:21.960
We've seen versions where like now you shoot lines of four instead of just two.

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:25.980
We've seen force fields and stuff like that.

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:37.640
So instead of that happening and having that as like a permanent kind of thing, instead you get the weapon select option, which is this separate menu where you choose your new ship based on which ships you've collected in the levels.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.240
Yeah. And there's a lot of different options.

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:41.640
Some that are really cool.

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:46.820
But to select them, you hit the select button, are brought into like a menu.

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:49.340
Your ship becomes a mouse.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:56.240
Yeah. You're now a cursor on like a bitmap of just all of the different shapes of the ships.

00:20:56.240 --> 00:21:03.840
And I guess it's just – I don't actually know how else they would have done this to be as clear as to what you're choosing.

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:07.740
I guess they could have just had press select until you get to what you want.

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:11.460
But it's an inelegant solution to a problem.

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:13.340
So I guess it's fine.

00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:16.660
For me, I did think of a solution for this.

00:21:16.860 --> 00:21:18.380
And I'm not saying that it's better.

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:22.260
I'm saying this was my offering as like I think that that's a really clunky way to do it.

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:23.460
It halts gameplay.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:29.800
It's pretty much like a pause screen where you get time to now just decide what you're going to pick and you're just like roaming.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.580
It's almost like immersion in the game.

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:33.760
If there is immersion in the game.

00:21:33.760 --> 00:21:39.880
It actually does break – it could be exploited now that I think about it because it does actually send you back a bit.

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:42.900
If you're about to die, you could just press the select button, I guess.

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:49.940
That's true. But I did notice too and I don't know if this was a lack of energy but there were certain times where I couldn't select stuff.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:57.860
So I don't know if that just has to do with like coming up on a boss now so you can't change or if I was actually just low on energy and unable to exchange it for power-ups.

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:04.720
But I think that if you made it so this way, the power-ups were actually just something that you collected, right?

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:13.360
Like if you wanted the octo ship version which is a really cool thing where bullets spread in all eight directions, right?

00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:14.320
Who wouldn't want that?

00:22:14.480 --> 00:22:16.180
It's something that you pick up on the map.

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:24.200
Your ship does like a cool little transformation slash fade maybe something simple into that new ship.

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:28.140
And now that's your ship until you collect the next power-up or die.

00:22:28.900 --> 00:22:30.920
Okay. I think that's one solution.

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:40.580
Another solution if you want to keep it up to choice is that when you're hitting the select button, you can cycle through the options while the game is still going.

00:22:40.740 --> 00:22:50.000
So you see the actual ship change designs because I think that was one super plus here if we're talking about like the low effort sprites being the letters and stuff like that.

00:22:50.220 --> 00:22:53.900
At least the ship looks different. At least the ship looks noticeably different and pretty cool.

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:55.560
There are some really cool ship designs in this one.

00:22:56.060 --> 00:22:58.440
I would have liked to just like toggle through that.

00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:04.780
The downside of that one is that it probably would require you to know which shape was which one you wanted.

00:23:05.180 --> 00:23:10.260
Yeah. Like you might know octo because of the way it looks, but are you going to know the difference between fire and thunder?

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:11.560
Maybe not. Yeah.

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:20.740
I don't particularly care for the inventory thing, but I think I still prefer it to at least in the way that way for what they're trying to do.

00:23:20.900 --> 00:23:22.480
I still think I prefer it to the other options.

00:23:22.480 --> 00:23:27.960
Like I would rather choose than have to cycle through while playing because then I feel like I would distract myself from playing.

00:23:28.180 --> 00:23:29.560
I would probably die doing that.

00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:34.240
How do you feel about it in Gradius where it was like, remember you were doing it all live and checking?

00:23:34.840 --> 00:23:39.940
I liked it, but I wouldn't have, I mean, I don't think I would have hated an inventory system.

00:23:40.120 --> 00:23:46.440
Granted, it is like you're giving up the immersion a little bit to break in, but like, I don't know.

00:23:46.520 --> 00:23:50.540
That happens in games. You got to pause to select a power up.

00:23:50.640 --> 00:24:00.860
It wasn't just a random bitmap with these ships spread around, but instead it was sort of, it was designed to look like a screen in your cockpit.

00:24:00.980 --> 00:24:03.820
Maybe that would be better for the immersion.

00:24:04.020 --> 00:24:05.480
Yeah. I don't hate that either.

00:24:05.480 --> 00:24:15.060
And I think even, you know, and I'm sorry that I didn't notice this while I was playing, but to your point about like, there's almost like a thing that says like you've, after you beat the boss that you're in the next stage.

00:24:15.220 --> 00:24:20.260
Yeah. If there's some kind of like docking sequence, we've seen that several times where you'll just dock somewhere and then come back up.

00:24:20.460 --> 00:24:24.980
And that's the only chance for you to pick your new machine for that level.

00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:29.220
Change the game up a lot, but that would be a cool gameplay element where it's like you have to plan a little bit.

00:24:29.220 --> 00:24:30.680
And then all you could, yeah.

00:24:30.900 --> 00:24:38.360
And then all you would need to do is press select and you would stop shooting like pew pew bullets and you could, you could, you could do your special ability with that.

00:24:38.620 --> 00:24:39.620
Which you chose. Yeah.

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:48.320
I think, I think one thing that I'm surprised about is that we haven't like, this is a creative use for the select button, but we haven't seen too many like super creative uses for the select button.

00:24:48.320 --> 00:24:57.000
And I'm not sure why, because like, yes, the start button should always be like a pause or a menu thing, but the select button should almost be treated like a third button in some cases, right?

00:24:57.000 --> 00:24:58.260
If you don't have anything else for it.

00:24:58.300 --> 00:24:59.760
Exactly. And it's kind of what this is.

00:24:59.960 --> 00:25:02.880
Yeah. It is like a third button to like cycle through menu.

00:25:03.140 --> 00:25:04.500
So I thought that was pretty cool.

00:25:04.860 --> 00:25:08.160
Yeah. Instead of actually using it to select what game mode.

00:25:08.200 --> 00:25:11.180
Yeah. It's strange to me that that was like a lot of times that was like the sole purpose.

00:25:11.180 --> 00:25:20.180
One full button of the what, six buttons that there are is just to, is just to select game A, game B.

00:25:20.780 --> 00:25:22.660
So let's talk about the different ships.

00:25:22.960 --> 00:25:27.120
I'll read off some descriptions and then I want you guys to tell me about which one you enjoyed the most.

00:25:27.540 --> 00:25:30.940
So we have Octo, which fired in eight different directions.

00:25:31.120 --> 00:25:34.660
It has the strongest lasers, but it's on a time limit.

00:25:35.120 --> 00:25:39.500
Then there's Shield, which creates a force field, which diminishes each time you are hit.

00:25:39.500 --> 00:25:42.140
So it's only as good as the force field lasts.

00:25:42.460 --> 00:25:47.340
Then you have Cannon, fires a powerful wide range laser, but has a time limit.

00:25:48.120 --> 00:25:51.480
Nuclear, which fires missiles with nuclear warheads.

00:25:51.780 --> 00:25:55.020
Each missile fired decreases your energy by four.

00:25:55.260 --> 00:25:57.460
So that one's more about keeping energy up.

00:25:57.480 --> 00:26:00.000
Otherwise you won't be able to shoot nuclear missiles.

00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:04.240
Homing fires guided missiles against ground targets.

00:26:04.240 --> 00:26:06.640
Each missile fired decreases energy by two.

00:26:06.820 --> 00:26:08.140
So again, in energy game.

00:26:08.140 --> 00:26:12.800
Fire, which shoots fire to destroy enemies, has a time limit.

00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:20.020
Time. Paralyzer, stops smaller enemies by firing a sword beam so they can be destroyed by smashing,

00:26:20.340 --> 00:26:21.480
has a time limit.

00:26:21.940 --> 00:26:23.100
And lastly, Thunder.

00:26:23.500 --> 00:26:26.200
Shoots lightning to destroy all enemies on screen.

00:26:26.460 --> 00:26:29.060
Each shot decreases energy by eight.

00:26:29.340 --> 00:26:30.620
The largest energy decrease.

00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:33.500
So guys, which one?

00:26:34.740 --> 00:26:36.720
I only use three.

00:26:37.340 --> 00:26:39.840
Okay. I played with Octo for a little bit.

00:26:40.400 --> 00:26:41.600
Got sick of it.

00:26:41.820 --> 00:26:44.140
I played with Thunder once.

00:26:44.400 --> 00:26:51.000
Thought it was neat. But if you're not using fire throughout this entire game, you're playing it wrong because it is so overpowered.

00:26:51.080 --> 00:26:56.540
It hits ships, ground targets, and projectiles.

00:26:57.420 --> 00:27:05.640
When you blow up any sort of item drop, you can just pick up energy there and it's just slowly refilling as you're expending.

00:27:05.900 --> 00:27:11.240
I was actually able to play through one full level with the fire going the entire time.

00:27:11.380 --> 00:27:12.200
Wow. Including the boss.

00:27:12.200 --> 00:27:13.420
And that one's on a time limit too.

00:27:13.520 --> 00:27:15.760
Yeah. That's interesting that they made the time limit that long.

00:27:16.060 --> 00:27:20.420
It was just that long. And if you just keep picking up energy, then it just adds to it.

00:27:20.580 --> 00:27:26.000
So I thought it kind of broke it for me because the boss wasn't even a boss at that point.

00:27:27.560 --> 00:27:31.500
But that was, I mean, it is empowering, I guess.

00:27:31.780 --> 00:27:32.720
Sure. Yeah.

00:27:32.940 --> 00:27:34.240
Joe, any thoughts on these?

00:27:34.420 --> 00:27:36.440
I mean, not really. To be honest, I didn't use a ton of them.

00:27:36.500 --> 00:27:38.280
I used fire and I used shield.

00:27:38.280 --> 00:27:41.600
I used shield, and I know I definitely tried a couple other ones, but...

00:27:41.600 --> 00:27:43.460
No Octo? I feel like everybody tries Octo.

00:27:43.460 --> 00:27:46.480
I think I did Octo as well, but nothing really stood out to me.

00:27:46.960 --> 00:27:49.520
I don't know, maybe it was also because I wasn't too high on the game anyways.

00:27:49.600 --> 00:27:51.420
Nothing stood out to me. It was like, oh, this one's perfect.

00:27:53.740 --> 00:27:58.220
Admittedly, I didn't play super far into this game where I feel like I need more power-ups.

00:27:58.320 --> 00:28:03.720
I think Octo is the one that is definitely the coolest if you're asking which one's really cool.

00:28:04.200 --> 00:28:07.020
But it's totally impractical when the bosses come around.

00:28:07.180 --> 00:28:09.700
Yeah. It's kind of useful.

00:28:09.900 --> 00:28:12.920
I don't even want to say it's super useful, even on the regular parts of the stage.

00:28:13.240 --> 00:28:18.360
Because it's this idea that you have a 360-degree spread now, but that spread's kind of weak.

00:28:18.640 --> 00:28:19.700
Yeah. It's not necessarily...

00:28:19.700 --> 00:28:22.180
You might be really close if you want to hit them with more than one.

00:28:22.320 --> 00:28:26.160
Right. It spreads out so far that there's a good chance you're going to miss most of the enemies.

00:28:26.340 --> 00:28:29.260
So I'm not saying Octo's actually the good choice.

00:28:29.260 --> 00:28:32.180
I thought it was the coolest looking slash working one.

00:28:32.360 --> 00:28:35.220
Yeah. Shield, I think it's a total waste of time.

00:28:35.220 --> 00:28:37.400
I think shield is maybe more of like a learning thing.

00:28:38.320 --> 00:28:41.400
And then there's like a bunch of ones in here that are like tricks.

00:28:41.760 --> 00:28:46.480
I think cannon, nuclear, homing, and paralyzer are all completely worthless.

00:28:47.120 --> 00:28:49.340
They are things that sound really cool on paper.

00:28:49.640 --> 00:28:50.740
Like homing, for instance.

00:28:50.740 --> 00:28:57.820
If I told you that you have the ability now in a shmup to fire guided missiles, there's a chance that you're going to want to get that.

00:28:58.040 --> 00:29:01.480
Yeah. But then you've got to remember that doesn't mean anything really in this game.

00:29:01.580 --> 00:29:02.920
That's against ground targets.

00:29:03.140 --> 00:29:04.620
They're not moving. They don't shoot very often.

00:29:04.780 --> 00:29:06.420
Yeah. You could hit them normally anyway.

00:29:06.420 --> 00:29:14.000
There are a few things like paralyzer or things like that that are cool in concept, but the game has to be designed in order for those to work.

00:29:14.120 --> 00:29:19.080
Very poor balance. Like the enemies have to, there have to be enemies that are like, oh, this is where you're going to want to use paralyzer.

00:29:19.300 --> 00:29:24.560
But like they really didn't, at least as far as I played, didn't like, there was nothing where I was like, oh, what do I need for these enemies?

00:29:25.200 --> 00:29:31.020
Right. I mean, like I give them, I give them complete kudos for like including all these power ups.

00:29:31.240 --> 00:29:38.000
